{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453093-predator-type-and-disciplines","id":1453093,"title":"Predator Type and Disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-21T17:00:13-07:00","id":1453093,"title":"Predator Type and Disciplines","content":"Okay. I'm just going to come right out and say it. I think it doesn't make sense from a gameplay perspective, a story perspective, or a mechanics perspective to give characters discipline dots with their predator type. Frankly I don't like it, and I'd like all of you not to like it with me lol<br /> <br /> First off, what disciplines you have from your embrace naturally will and should influence your predator type and that makes sense. <br /> <br /> Gameplay wise you are just giving out-of-clan disciplines away with little to no explanation. Now some might say the explanation is that you have been, say for ally cat, needing to be quick or strong and so celerity or potence makes sense. And it would, but you need to be trained and sucking the blood of another kindred who has these disciplines first. <br /> <br /> From a game mechanics view you can get a 3rd lvl dot for free if you play it right, and that is pretty nice bait for people to lean in that direction. And I see it all the time. Which just cuts back on diversity because every other tremere will be a bagger and every other toreador will be a siren or a scene queen etc. Its also pretty unfair for a game where exp is meant to be kinda rare to just be throwin 15exp around.<br /> <br /> Another mechanical issue is thin-bloods get left out of this on EVERY level really, because now even though these kindred SHOULD have a preferred way of getting blood, if they are still alive at this point, they somehow don't know how to feed themselves? And this is something I see a lot too, people wanting to play a pretty interesting thin-blood character but don't because they miss out on a PT.<br /> <br /> I like predator styles a lot, I think they add depth to a kindreds night-to-night life. But these disciplines are boggin it down. Let me know what you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T18:14:15-07:00","id":1453096,"title":"","content":"I do find the options a little constricting. What if I want my Gangrel to be an Alleycat, but it wins these fights with the bums it's eating by being too tough to hurt, or by having its pet hold them down? What if my Bagger Tremere wants to use Dominate to make security give it the bagged blood? What if my Blood Leech charms other vampire into selling their blood to it relatively cheap via Presence?<br /> <br /> In my games I've dumped Predator types and just give players an extra dot in their clan disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-21-2021, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T19:38:16-07:00","id":1453105,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of them is OK, and I actually like that they stem from character personality. The whole You Are What You Eat, stuff also helps explain the Disciplines a bit on the story side of things.<br /> <br /> But the packages are poorly designed across the board, and the Discipline part makes them a huge sticking point for a char-gen system that otherwise smooths out optimization bumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T23:59:46-07:00","id":1453116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453093-predator-type-and-disciplines?p=1453105#post1453105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea of them is OK, and I actually like that they stem from character personality. The whole You Are What You Eat, stuff also helps explain the Disciplines a bit on the story side of things.<br /> <br /> But the packages are poorly designed across the board, and the Discipline part makes them a huge sticking point for a char-gen system that otherwise smooths out optimization bumps.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you do them, Heavy? I like them in theory, but like you, think the packages are poorly designed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T00:12:22-07:00","id":1453117,"title":"","content":"The real silly moment is where they've decided vampires get disciplines from resonances but also how they hunt is relevant. <br /> <br /> Disciplines being related to how how the vampire hunts seems completely natural, given that clan disciplines align perfectly with how you expect these vampires to normally hunt. <br /> <br /> &quot;predator types&quot; are, however, a mechanical shitshow. Character creation in V5 is so tightly controlled up till this point, so that nobody can get an unreasonable advantage through clever alocations, and then you can throw on a predator type and BOOM, that tight control has been upended. The options available are also extremely limited and don't grasp the normal diversity many vampires need; While &quot;siren&quot; can function 90% of the time, nobody's going to be an alleycat 90% of the time and expect to live long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T00:44:16-07:00","id":1453118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453093-predator-type-and-disciplines?p=1453117#post1453117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real silly moment is where they've decided vampires get disciplines from resonances but also how they hunt is relevant.<br /> <br /> Disciplines being related to how how the vampire hunts seems completely natural, given that clan disciplines align perfectly with how you expect these vampires to normally hunt.<br /> <br /> &quot;predator types&quot; are, however, a mechanical shitshow. Character creation in V5 is so tightly controlled up till this point, so that nobody can get an unreasonable advantage through clever alocations, and then you can throw on a predator type and BOOM, that tight control has been upended. The options available are also extremely limited and don't grasp the normal diversity many vampires need; While &quot;siren&quot; can function 90% of the time, nobody's going to be an alleycat 90% of the time and expect to live long.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the WOD I do think an Alleycat could survive, since they is much more poverty and apathy than the real world. However, such a vampire would be restricted to either the parts of the city with the most crime and poverty, or the open road, i.e. eating hitchickers and wandering hobos. Which means you'd pretty much expect this to be the technique of Nos, Gangrel, and some of the less socially adept Brujah.<br /> <br /> Really Blood Leech is the biggest stretch. Someone is either going to kill it, or blood bond it pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-22-2021, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T01:20:40-07:00","id":1453120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453093-predator-type-and-disciplines?p=1453116#post1453116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you do them, Heavy? I like them in theory, but like you, think the packages are poorly designed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make them more DIY with some set guidelines; basically like how Abilities have a few options for how to spread things out, and you pick where your dots go.<br /> <br /> A few basic templates built with a base of what the value of the Discipline would be means you can keep the XP values the same; as well as have things like more options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T13:00:37-07:00","id":1453200,"title":"","content":"Trying to work with the strict character creation of V5 for maximum balance, while trying to keep things simple. <br /> -Pick an out of clan discipline, or the in-clan discipline you didn't pick with 2/1/0. If choosing the in-clan discipline, gain a couple background points to make up the difference in XP (Your talent means less time struggling to get food and more time accumulating the goods.. is how I'd fluff it. ) <br /> -Choose from a short list of merits or backgrounds tied to the hunting style that cultivates that discipline. Presence might come with good looks, allies, fame etc. <br /> -Choose from a short list of flaws. Ditto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T11:28:14-07:00","id":1453302,"title":"","content":"Here's how I would do it:<br /> <br /> Think of a predator style you feel like you could pull off in real life. How would your embrace given disciplines help you with this strategy? Why don't you get caught?<br /> -You get 1 skill specialty connected to this style (or 1 dot if you don't have the skill).<br /> -You also get 1 merit connected to this style.<br /> -Your storyteller will choose 1 Flaw of equal dots that is a result of your favored style of feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}